# AgentKeep TypeScript conventions

- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any`.  
- Money: integer minor units only; never floats.  
- Errors: throw/map to catalog `error.code`; include `request_id`.  
- Payment verify behind an interface; mock in tests by default.  
- SSRF logic lives in shared package; unit-test with table-driven cases.  
- Do not log memory values, payment headers, OTP codes, or session tokens.  
- Prefer pure functions for pricing, credit application, resource hashing — easy unit tests.  
- DB: wallet row locks / transactions for cap + credit updates.  
- Controllers thin; business logic in services.
